{"words": [{"text": "فَتَلَقَّىٰٓ", "translation": "Then received"}, {"text": "ءَادَمُ", "translation": "Adam"}, {"text": "مِن", "translation": "from"}, {"text": "رَّبِّهِۦ", "translation": "his Lord"}, {"text": "كَلِمَـٰتٍۢ", "translation": "words"}, {"text": "فَتَابَ", "translation": "So (his Lord) turned"}, {"text": "عَلَيْهِ ۚ", "translation": "towards him"}, {"text": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translation": "Indeed He"}, {"text": "هُوَ", "translation": "He"}, {"text": "ٱلتَّوَّابُ", "translation": "(is) the Oft-returning (to mercy)"}, {"text": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translation": "the Most Merciful"}], "sahih": "Then Adam received from his Lord [some] words,1 and He accepted his repentance. Indeed, it is He who is the Accepting of Repentance,2 the Merciful."}